  "id": "near-miss",
  "term": "near miss",
  "definition": "In this source, a near miss means a severe event affecting a pregnant or childbirth-related patient that is survived, and it is often discussed alongside severe maternal morbidity. The term is used for monitoring serious complications because studying these cases may help reduce illness and death.",
